# Pagination

Navigation between pages of results. Compose it from `Pagination`, `PaginationContent`, `PaginationItem`, `PaginationLink`, `PaginationPrevious`, `PaginationNext`, and `PaginationEllipsis`.

<Demo />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Pagination, PaginationContent, PaginationItem, PaginationLink, PaginationPrevious, PaginationNext, PaginationEllipsis } from "#lib/components/ui/pagination/index.js";
</script>

<Pagination>
	<PaginationContent>
		<PaginationItem><PaginationPrevious href="?page=1" /></PaginationItem>
		<PaginationItem><PaginationLink href="?page=1">1</PaginationLink></PaginationItem>
		<PaginationItem><PaginationLink href="?page=2" isActive>2</PaginationLink></PaginationItem>
		<PaginationItem><PaginationLink href="?page=3">3</PaginationLink></PaginationItem>
		<PaginationItem><PaginationEllipsis /></PaginationItem>
		<PaginationItem><PaginationNext href="?page=3" /></PaginationItem>
	</PaginationContent>
</Pagination>
```

## Installation

```pm
npx remote0 add https://plainsv.com/r/pagination.json
```

## Anatomy

`Pagination` renders a `nav` landmark labeled `pagination`, and `PaginationContent` a list of `PaginationItem` entries. `PaginationLink`, `PaginationPrevious`, and `PaginationNext` render a `Button`: an `a` with `href`, so SvelteKit navigates on the client, or a `button` with `onclick` for state-driven pages. Set `isActive` on the current page to outline it and mark it with `aria-current="page"`. The previous and next labels hide on narrow screens, and their `aria-label` keeps them named. `PaginationEllipsis` marks a gap, read as "More pages".

## Page range

`getPageRange(currentPage, pageCount, siblingCount)` returns the pages to show around the current page, with `"ellipsis"` for the gaps. The first and last pages are always shown, and `siblingCount` sets how many pages show on each side of the current one; the default is `1`.

<Demo section="controlled" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Pagination, PaginationContent, PaginationItem, PaginationLink, PaginationPrevious, PaginationNext, PaginationEllipsis, getPageRange } from "#lib/components/ui/pagination/index.js";

	const pageCount = 20;
	let currentPage = $state(8);
	const pages = $derived(getPageRange(currentPage, pageCount));
</script>

<Pagination>
	<PaginationContent>
		<PaginationItem><PaginationPrevious disabled={currentPage === 1} onclick={() => currentPage--} /></PaginationItem>
		{#each pages as page, index (index)}
			<PaginationItem>
				{#if page === "ellipsis"}
					<PaginationEllipsis />
				{:else}
					<PaginationLink isActive={page === currentPage} onclick={() => (currentPage = page)}>{page}</PaginationLink>
				{/if}
			</PaginationItem>
		{/each}
		<PaginationItem><PaginationNext disabled={currentPage === pageCount} onclick={() => currentPage++} /></PaginationItem>
	</PaginationContent>
</Pagination>
```

## Sizes

Set `size` on `Pagination` to `xs`, `sm`, `md`, or `lg`. The default is `md`, and every link and the ellipsis follow it.

<Demo section="sizes" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Pagination size="sm">...</Pagination>
```

## Overrides

`PaginationLink`, `PaginationPrevious`, and `PaginationNext` take their own `size`, which wins over the pagination's for that link only. They also pass `rounded` to their button.

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<PaginationItem>
	<PaginationLink href="#" isActive size="lg" rounded="pill">2</PaginationLink>
</PaginationItem>
```

## API

`Pagination`, `PaginationContent`, and `PaginationItem` extend the native `nav`, `ul`, and `li` attributes. `PaginationLink`, `PaginationPrevious`, and `PaginationNext` take the `Button` props, except `size` and `variant`.

```ts title="index.ts"
interface Props extends CompPropsWithChild<"nav"> {
	/** Link size on the shared scale; defaults to `md` */
	size?: UiSize;
}

type LinkProps = ButtonAttrs & {
	/** Marks the current page with an outline and `aria-current="page"` */
	isActive?: boolean;
	children: Snippet;
	/** Size of this square link; overrides the pagination's `size` */
	size?: UiSize;
};

type StepProps = ButtonAttrs & {
	/** Label beside the chevron; defaults to `Previous` or `Next` */
	children?: Snippet;
	/** Size of this link; overrides the pagination's `size` */
	size?: UiSize;
};

function getPageRange(currentPage: number, pageCount: number, siblingCount?: number): (number | "ellipsis")[];
```
